                <pb facs="0303" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Evenson, B./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-25T11:00:00+08:00">October 25, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 25—3:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>100. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 25, 11 a.m. My October 24, 3 p.m. Telegram from Sinyangchow
                            states Miss Evenson has been released. Nelson and Tvedt are still
                            held.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department and Nanking.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
